 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- Spool compaction deletes each merge group's inputs as soon as the group's
+  merged run is fsynced. Peak scratch usage is therefore bounded by one
+  merge group at every stage, including seal: the old 2x (all remaining
+  runs + full sealed output) high-water mark at seal time is gone.
